WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.290
Act 2.

2
00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:04.400
Polished Gerald Croft
admits he knew the girl,

3
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:07.200
under another name: Daisy Renton.

4
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:10.250
He met her at a theatre bar in March 1911,

5
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.820
and rescued her from an
alderman's unwanted attention.

6
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.700
On one side of the scales: a helping hand,

7
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.810
a key, some coins.

8
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.450
On the other, a question mark.

9
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.770
Of everyone, Gerald was kindest to Eva.

10
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.020
Does that make him less guilty?

11
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.180
In this mission, you'll hear
his story of Daisy Renton,

12
00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.320
as he tells it in Act 2.

13
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.220
You'll meet the woman
at the centre of it all,

14
00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.870
who never once appears on stage.

15
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.360
And you'll follow Gerald into Act
3, where the scales are tested.

16
00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:45.970
Your mission: decide whether Gerald's
kindness makes him less guilty.
